        "runId": "ada-en-mw8vshb5-enc7ju",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Petrópolis to Rio de Janeiro"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "8ac665949e7b8ecf906be5a866e34cb6d2dae9d828f39f153948f2ec9d288507",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw8vshb5-enc7ju",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Take a sightseeing tour of Petrópolis, with lunch at Cervejaria Bohemia.\n\nThe city lies in the mountains about 60 km from Rio. Its history is tied to Emperor Pedro II and the summer residence built in 1830. The Imperial Palace is now a museum housing decorative art, furniture, old books, statues of saints and the imperial crown worn at the coronation, set with diamonds and pearls. Petrópolis is a stop for history between the mountain roads of Minas Gerais and a full day in Rio.\n\nThe city's German architectural heritage is visible in houses with tall windows, attic storeys and steeply pitched roofs. The tour focuses on imperial history and local architecture, with lunch at Cervejaria Bohemia along the way. After the tour, continue to Rio de Janeiro.\n\n**Approximate distance:** 260 km.  \n**Hotel:** Arena Copacabana."
    },
